From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:36:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mark the pthread worker callback noexcept for Cython 3

The hunspell/hunspell.cpp shipped in the 2.0.2 tag was generated by
Cython 0.29.21 and #includes "longintrepr.h", a header CPython removed
in 3.11, so it cannot be compiled for any interpreter this repo builds
(cp312+). The build regenerates it from hunspell.pyx with Cython 3,
which supports CPython 3.12-3.14 and free-threaded builds.

Cython 3 makes non-extern cdef functions propagate exceptions by
default, so hunspell_worker becomes `except? NULL` and no longer
matches the `void *(*)(void *)` (implicitly noexcept) function pointer
that thread_create() takes:

  hunspell.pyx:504:43: Cannot assign type 'void *(*)(void *) except? NULL
  nogil' to 'void *(*)(void *) noexcept'. Exception values are
  incompatible.

The worker runs on a bare pthread with no GIL and never raises, so
declaring it `noexcept` restores the exact 0.29 semantics. The keyword
is accepted by Cython >= 0.29.31 too.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [upstream inactive since 2.0.2 (2021); no fork of MSeal/cython_hunspell to push from]
---
 hunspell/hunspell.pyx | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hunspell/hunspell.pyx b/hunspell/hunspell.pyx
index 9c4ae48..dff1f50 100644
--- a/hunspell/hunspell.pyx
+++ b/hunspell/hunspell.pyx
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ cdef struct ThreadWorkerArgs:
     # Determines if the thread is executing a stem or suggestion callback
     action_type action_e
 
-cdef void *hunspell_worker(void *argument) nogil:
+cdef void *hunspell_worker(void *argument) noexcept nogil:
     cdef ThreadWorkerArgs args
     cdef int i
     args = deref(<ThreadWorkerArgs *>argument)
